{
  peppy_schema: "launcher/v1",
  description: [
    "A simulation on its own: the engine and its viewer, standing no robot, for a machine whose job is the simulation and nothing else. Isaac Sim needs an NVIDIA GPU.",
    "`peppy stack launch simulation`: Waldo and its viewer.",
    "`peppy stack launch simulation --with isaac_sim`: Isaac Sim and the browser frontend of its WebRTC livestream.",
    "`peppy stack launch simulation --with web_scene_commander`: the scene panel with it.",
    "The simulation runs on the machine the launch is sent to: this one, or the one `--core-node` names. Waldo serves its viewer and the hand teleop panel on viewer_port (8080) and Isaac Sim its WebRTC frontend on 8210. The scene panel, on 8766, is the axis each of them declares, so it takes the launch word web_scene_commander: spawn, move and remove objects, and list what stands in the scene.",
    "This launcher declares no robot axis, so nothing joins it. A robot stands in a simulation the same launch names, which is what the launchers openarm_simulation, so101_simulation and simulation_mcp do.",
    "MuJoCo is no option here: it answers no scene call, so nothing in this launch could command it. It runs a robot's own simulation in those launchers.",
  ],

  components: [
    {
      name: "simulation",
      cardinality: "one",
      options: {
        isaac_sim: "fragments/isaac_sim.json5",
        waldo: "fragments/waldo.json5",
      },
    },
  ],

  deployments: [
    { simulation: "waldo" },
  ],
}
